{# Decrypt-on-view fragment (design D4) swapped into #csam-meta-<id> by the per-row
   "Decrypt metadata" button. Surfaces ONLY scalar metadata fields from the AES-256-GCM
   blob — the uploader's raw pseudonymous internal UUID (intended, design D4), the
   affected post id, the source, and the cascade count. There is NO image-bytes / content
   URL field by construction (design D3); the archive never stored image bytes.

   Every decrypt that reaches this fragment was role-gated (owner/admin) + CSRF-checked
   and is recorded as exactly one csam_metadata_decrypted audit row — including the
   fail-soft `unavailable` case (key unset / encrypted_metadata NULL → no 500). All
   values are Pebble-autoescaped. #}
{% if unavailable %}
<p class="outcome-message muted">{{ message }}</p>
{% else %}
<dl class="kv">
    <dt>Uploader user id</dt><dd><span class="code">{{ uploaderUserId }}</span></dd>
    <dt>Affected post id</dt><dd><span class="code">{{ affectedPostId }}</span></dd>
    <dt>Source</dt><dd>{{ source }}</dd>
    <dt>Posts cascade-tombstoned</dt><dd>{{ cascadeCount }}</dd>
    <dd class="note">Decrypted on demand. This view is audit-logged; no image content is ever revealed.</dd>
</dl>
{% endif %}
